# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# House folder convention
#
# A leading dot means "not part of the product". Two kinds:
#   TRACKED   .plans/    design notes for work in flight (committed; they are the
#                        record of why a change was made the way it was)
#             .claude/skills/  project skills (shared with whoever works here)
#             .cargo/ .github/ .vscode/   tooling config
#   IGNORED   .output/   dump folder for script/util byproducts: query results,
#                        summary stats, graphs, run logs. Created by `just setup`;
#                        scripts assume it exists and do not mkdir it. Anything a
#                        recipe writes as a byproduct points here, never at the
#                        repo root or cwd.
#             .test_output/ .temp/ .venv/ deploy/ .website/
#
# Ignore lines below are grouped to match. Add the folder to BOTH this file and
# the `just clean` recipe, or `clean` starts lying.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# dump folder for script/util output (query results, stats, graphs, run logs)
.output/

# staged website output (both tiers)
deploy/
.website/

# test byproducts
.test_output/
.misc_test_output/

# the original game's files, wherever they land: never ours to redistribute
*.DAT
*.EXE
*.ISO

# archeology: not ours to redistribute, only the findings are
achieve/*
# !achieve/report.md
# !achieve/scan_all.sh

# reverse engineering workspace. Our own scripts, notes and recovered C are tracked; the
# downloaded toolchain, the third party reference checkout and every derived artefact are
# not. Nothing here is ours to redistribute except the findings.
reversing/.tools/
reversing/.ref/
reversing/.venv/
reversing/work/

# my convention for scratch that is not worth naming
.temp/
temp/
# agent scratch, at any depth
scratchpad/

# ai assistants: share skills with whoever works here, keep personal settings local
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Rust builds a target, big and fat,
# We don't want to carry that.
/target/
/**/*.rs.bk
# utils/ crates sit outside the workspace, so /target/ above does not reach them.
# Their Cargo.lock IS tracked: a tool that stops building on someone else's minor
# release is a tool you will not fix at the moment you need it.
utils/*/target/
landscape_shader/target/

# huge profiler droppings
perf.data
perf.data.*

# logs and crash reports
logs/

# Python caches in a sneaky way,
# But they don't belong, no, not today.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.manifest
*.spec
*.log

# jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# venvs
.venv/
.venv_linux/
env/
ENV/
venv/

# node explodes
node_modules/

# VSCode: settings/tasks/launch are shared, the rest is personal
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# Mac and Windows scat
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Icon?
Desktop.ini

# editor scat
*.sublime*
*.code-workspace
.idea/

# temp files
*.bak
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*.old
*.png~
*.jpg~
*.jpeg~
*.webp~
*.gif~

# internal shit
diff.patch

# secrets
*.env
.env.*
!.upstash.env.example

# derived web images (regenerated by scripts/web/auto_images.sh; leaving stale
# copies in the repo interferes with their recreation in CI)
web/auto_*/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public mirror only. scripts/git/publish_public.sh appends this file to .gitignore to decide what reaches the public
# repo: anything tracked here that these rules (or the regular ones) ignore stays private.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# the reversing pass: the recovered C is not ours to redistribute
reversing/

# the owner's notes
.plans/
todo.md

# personal editor config
.vscode/
